From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libipa: camera_sensor_helper: Add ov13b10, ov8856 and s5k5e9

The Lenovo Tab P12 Pro (TB-Q706F, SM8250) has three camera sensors that
libcamera 0.7.0 has no CameraSensorHelper for: ov13b10 (main rear),
s5k5e9 (second rear) and ov8856 (front). Without a helper the software
ISP of the "simple" pipeline works on raw V4L2 gain codes instead of
linear gains and logs "Failed to create camera sensor helper".

Gain models, all linear, taken from the Linux 7.3.4 sensor drivers
(drivers/media/i2c/):

  ov13b10  OV13B10_ANA_GAIN_MIN 0x80, MAX 0x7c0, STEP 1; register 0x3508
           holds gain * 128 (0x80 = 1x)          -> code / 128
  ov8856   OV8856_ANAL_GAIN_MIN 128, MAX 2047, STEP 1, same register
           layout as ov13b10/ov5675/ov13858       -> code / 128
  s5k5e9   V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN 32..1024 written to the SMIA register
           analogue_gain_code_global (0x0204); code 32 = 1x as on other
           Samsung SMIA sensors (inferred, no datasheet) -> code / 32

Black level (16-bit scale):

  ov8856   4096: the driver programs the BLC target register 0x4003 = 0x40
           (64 at 10 bits), the same source as the existing ov5675 helper.
  ov13b10, s5k5e9: not set. The drivers do not program a BLC target and
           no datasheet value is available, so the software ISP keeps
           estimating the black level from the histogram.

Not upstream. Local patch for the q706f Ubuntu port.
---
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -753,6 +753,19 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov64a40", CameraSensorHelperOv64a40)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperOv8856 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperOv8856()
+	{
+		/* From Linux kernel driver: 0x40 at 10bits (BLC target 0x4003). */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		/* Linux kernel driver: code 128 = 1x, 1/128 steps up to 2047. */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 128 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov8856", CameraSensorHelperOv8856)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperOv8858 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
@@ -789,6 +802,36 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov13858", CameraSensorHelperOv13858)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperOv13b10 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperOv13b10()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Linux kernel driver: code 0x80 = 1x, 1/128 steps up to 0x7c0.
+		 * The driver does not program the BLC target; leave the black
+		 * level unset so that the IPA keeps estimating it.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 128 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov13b10", CameraSensorHelperOv13b10)
+
+class CameraSensorHelperS5k5e9 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperS5k5e9()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * SMIA-style analogue_gain_code_global (0x0204): the Linux kernel
+		 * driver exposes 32..1024 with code 32 = 1x, as for other Samsung
+		 * SMIA sensors. Black level unknown, left to the IPA estimate.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 32 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("s5k5e9", CameraSensorHelperS5k5e9)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperVd55g1 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
